  "exit": 0,
  "said": "Lent jellyfin (port 8096) to everyone in your groups, as many at once as want it. To let fewer in at once, change it on your home page, or `svrngs share 8096 --limit <number>`.\nEach person is signed in to it as themselves by what answers on port 8097, with nothing typed.\nsvrngs is running here already, so they can open it now.\n`svrngs unshare jellyfin` stops lending it.",
  "ms": 10
 },
 "ana_join": {
  "who": "ana",
  "args": [
   "join",
   "http://localhost:50196/#<the token>",
   "--as",
   "Ana",
   "--no-run"
  ],
  "exit": 0,
  "said": "You're in two, as Ana.\ntwo's folder is /tmp/two-run/ana/svrngs/two: what anyone in two puts there reaches this computer, and what you put there reaches theirs.",
  "ms": 2314
 },
 "ana_device_link_said": "A link that adds another computer or phone of yours to two: open it there, and it joins as you, Ana, asked no name. Send it to nobody else: whoever opens it joins as you. Any link you sent before stops letting anyone new in; everyone it let in stays.\nA computer or phone already in two on its own stays as it joined.\nIt works for a day, while this computer is on:\n\n  svrngs://join/<the token>\n\nor, to open it in a browser:\n\n  http://localhost:50196/#<the token>\n\nOn a phone, each app opens at an address of its own under localhost:50196, which can see which app is opened.\n\nLeave this running; Ctrl-C stops it.",
 "laptop_join": {
  "said": "You're in two, as Ana.",
